ta.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/frusg/FRUSG_2024.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-annual/SchedulesFederalDebt_Annual_2024.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n- 2025-06-18 — Treasury’s *Debt to the Penny* dataset page says it is **released daily**, with data current through **2025-06-17** on that page snapshot, and describes total public debt as composed of Treasury bills, notes, bonds, TIPS, FRNs, and other Treasury securities. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/debt-to-the-penny/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/debt-to-the-penny/?utm_source=openai))\n\nI did **not** find a Treasury Fiscal Data page for **September 2026** specifically; the most recent relevant Treasury Fiscal Data result I found for this topic was **July 31, 2025**. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf?utm_source=openai))"
