    "url": "https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/interest-expense-avg-interest-rates/",
    "title": null,
    "published": null,
    "text": "Last Updated: --\nInterest Expense is the interest the government pays on its outstanding loans (Treasury securities). It can be referred to as the cost to the U.S. for borrowing money. The amount of interest expense depends on the total federal debt and the interest rates investors charged when they loaned the money. Average interest rates are a useful measure for showing general trends in the interest the government pays on its loans, even though the true cost of the loans will vary by security type and by the interest rate for those securities when the loan was taken. To see a breakdown of average rates by security, visit the Average Interest Rates on U.S. Treasury Securities dataset."
